/ tagged-evidence (key 0) is present but is a tstr rather than                /
/ [ 1*8 tagged-concise-evidence ]. Unlike the optional members, key 0 is      /
/ mandatory in spdm-toc-map, so zcbor decodes it with an expect instead of a  /
/ present_decode: the whole map decode hard-fails and the value can never     /
/ backtrack into the extension array. This fixture pins that invariant, so    /
/ omitting key 0 from kSpdmTocSchemaKeys stays correct.                       /
570({
  / tagged-evidence / 0: "not-a-list-of-concise-evidence",
  / profile / 2: 32("http://example.com/profile")
})
